      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1174221975">
          <groundspeak:date>2023-06-13T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP425 Cochrane Event [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today my wanderings took me past both of the listed brass caps in the Waiparous area. I knew about the difficult one which I decided not to try, but then I also accidentally flew by the easy one without even realizing it. Oops. Feeling bad about all of that, I contented myself with getting this one on the way back home. Still eroding but still there! &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684620765">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6304346">sapien</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP425 Cochrane Event

N 51° 11.161 W 114° 29.178&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I wasn't sure which was the best way to approach this cap  I ended up approaching from the northwest direction; I have no idea if the other way(s) would have been easier or not.  I sure hope the erosion at GZ doesn't take this cap with it.  I was a bit concerned about my safety but it turned out to be a non-issue.  Most of the information from the cap is readable after a close examination.  TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683871536">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP425 - Cochrane Event - Iron Phoenix wisely told me not to park on the highway and walk up :) I would have missed the lawn chair chained to a tree if I had done that :) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Phoenix and I spent the day continuing our Calgary and area capping spree. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682463368">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1636194">behmSquad</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP425 Cochrane Event&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I'm down to a final day to add to my large cap haul this month. This cap would be one of twelve that I found this afternoon pushing my total for the month into three digits. Today was focused on a few caps on the western outskirts of Calgary and those in and around Cochrane.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I heard about this cap during my last breakfast event nearby.  I had other plans for the day then which left it to be a part of this big cap day.  No problem finding it.  Thanks for the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682020693">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7573673">geoCurious2</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP425 - Cochrane Event&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were out in Cochrane for our granddaughter's baseball game and decided to pick up some Brass Caps while we still could!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
